    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>A sequence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_1, u_2, u_3 \\ldots\"></span> is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u_1=35\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u_{n+1}=u_n+7\\cos\\left(\\frac{n\\pi}{2}\\right)-5(-1)^n\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_2=40\"></span></li><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_3\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_4\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the sequence is periodic with order 4</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>write down the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_5\"></span></li><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^{25}u_r\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
