    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>Coffee is poured into a cup.</p><p>The temperature of the coffee, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after being poured into the cup is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"H=A\\mathrm e^{-Bt}+30\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants.</p><p>Initially, the temperature of the coffee was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"85\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Initially, the coffee was cooling at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7.5\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C\"></span> per minute.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Find a complete equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>, giving the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
