    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span></p><p>The curve</p><ul><li>passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(3,-10)\"></span></li><li>has a turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span></li></ul><p>Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}=2x^3-9x^2+5x+k\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=12\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence find the coordinates of the point where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
