    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>Relative to a fixed origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>,</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is the point with position vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\mathbf i\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> is the point with position vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16\\mathbf j\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is the point with position vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(50\\mathbf i+136\\mathbf j)\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\"></span> is the point with position vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(22\\mathbf i+24\\mathbf j)\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD\"></span> is parallel to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\"></span> are used to model the vertices of a running track in the shape of a quadrilateral.</p><p>Runners complete one lap by running along all four sides of the track.</p><p>The lengths of the sides are measured in metres.</p><p>Given that a particular runner takes exactly 5 minutes to complete 2 laps,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>calculate the average speed of this runner, giving the answer in kilometres per hour. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
