    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q7",
      "question": "<p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><p>A curve has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3+2xy+3y^2=47\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-2,5)\"></span> lies on the curve.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Find the equation of the normal to the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by+c=0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
