    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q8",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\cos\\theta+8\\sin\\theta\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\\cos(\\theta-\\alpha)\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> are constants, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R&gt;0\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\alpha&lt;\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\"></span><p>Give the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> and give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> in radians to 3 decimal places.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The first three terms of an arithmetic sequence are</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos x\\qquad\\cos x+\\sin x\\qquad\\cos x+2\\sin x\\qquad x\\neq n\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_9\"></span> represents the sum of the first 9 terms of this sequence as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> varies,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>find the exact maximum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_9\"></span></li><li>deduce the smallest positive value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> at which this maximum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_9\"></span> occurs.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
