      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q11",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:100mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. A cuboid tank with base 20 m by 10 m and height 5 m, partly filled with water to a depth of h m (shaded).\"></figure><p>A tank in the shape of a cuboid is being filled with water.</p><p>The base of the tank measures <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> and the height of the tank is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>, as shown in Figure 1.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after water started flowing into the tank the height of the water was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> and the volume of water in the tank was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\\,\\mathrm m^3\"></span></p><p>In a model of this situation</p><ul><li>the sides of the tank have negligible thickness</li><li>the rate of change of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is inversely proportional to the square root of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dh}{\\mathrm dt}=\\frac{\\lambda}{\\sqrt h}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> is a constant.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that</p><ul><li>initially the height of the water in the tank was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.44\\,\\mathrm m\"></span></li><li>exactly 8 minutes after water started flowing into the tank the height of the water was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3.24\\,\\mathrm m\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>use the model to find an equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>, giving your answer in the form<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h^{\\frac{3}{2}}=At+B\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence find the time taken, from when water started flowing into the tank, for the tank to be completely full. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
