      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:90mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q12-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Sketch of N against t for 0 to 5 years: N_A is a V-shaped graph with its minimum at t = 3; N_B is an inverted V-shaped graph with its maximum at t = 3; the graphs cross twice.\"></figure><p>The number of subscribers to two different music streaming companies is being monitored.</p><p>The number of subscribers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm A}\"></span>, in thousands, to <strong>company A</strong> is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm A}=|t-3|+4\\qquad t\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the time in years since monitoring began.</p><p>The number of subscribers, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm B}\"></span>, in thousands, to <strong>company B</strong> is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm B}=8-|2t-6|\\qquad t\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the time in years since monitoring began.</p><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm A}\"></span> and the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm B}\"></span> over a 5-year period.</p><p><strong>Use the equations of the models to answer parts (a), (b), (c) and (d).</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the initial difference between the number of subscribers to <strong>company A</strong> and the number of subscribers to <strong>company B</strong>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=T\"></span> <strong>company A</strong> reduced its subscription prices and the number of subscribers increased.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Suggest a value for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, giving a reason for your answer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find the range of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N_{\\mathrm A}&gt;N_{\\mathrm B}\"></span> giving your answer in set notation. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>State a limitation of the model used for <strong>company B</strong>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
