      "question": "<p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the first three terms, in ascending powers of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>, of the binomial expansion of<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3+x)^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>writing each term in simplest form.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Using the answer to part (a) and using algebraic integration, estimate the value of<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_{0.2}^{0.4}\\frac{6x}{(3+x)^2}\\,\\mathrm dx\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your answer to 4 significant figures.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Find, using algebraic integration, the exact value of<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_{0.2}^{0.4}\\frac{6x}{(3+x)^2}\\,\\mathrm dx\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\ln b+c\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
