      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q14",
      "question": "<p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\tan\\theta\\left(8\\cos\\theta+23\\sin^2\\theta\\right)=8\\sin2\\theta\\left(1+\\tan^2\\theta\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>may be written as</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin2\\theta\\left(A\\cos^2\\theta+B\\cos\\theta+C\\right)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Hence, solve for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\leqslant x\\leqslant540^\\circ\"></span><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\tan x\\left(8\\cos x+23\\sin^2x\\right)=8\\sin2x\\left(1+\\tan^2x\\right)\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R\\quad x\\neq450^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
