      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2023-june/q15",
      "question": "<p>A student attempts to answer the following question:</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><td><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> is an obtuse angle, use algebra to prove by contradiction that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin x-\\cos x\\geqslant1\" data-display=\"true\"></div></td></tr></table><p>The student starts the proof with:</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><td><p>Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin x-\\cos x&lt;1\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> is an obtuse angle</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(\\sin x-\\cos x)^2&lt;1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></div></td></tr></table><p>The start of the student’s proof is reprinted below.</p><p>Complete the proof. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>Assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin x-\\cos x&lt;1\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> is an obtuse angle</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(\\sin x-\\cos x)^2&lt;1\" data-display=\"true\"></div>",
